From: CAOS <caos@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nscd_query: treat a missing socket syscall as "no nscd"

musl's getgrouplist() (and therefore initgroups(), and therefore BusyBox
`su`, `login` and `id NAME`) first asks nscd over an AF_UNIX socket.

__nscd_query() already tolerates a kernel that has no AF_UNIX support by
treating EAFNOSUPPORT as "nscd is not running".  CAOS builds its kernel with
CONFIG_NET=n, which removes net/socket.c entirely: every socket-related
syscall is then routed to sys_ni_syscall() and fails with ENOSYS instead of
EAFNOSUPPORT.  musl treated that as a hard error, so getgrouplist() failed
with ENOSYS and BusyBox reported:

    su: can't set groups: Function not implemented

Treat ENOSYS the same way as EAFNOSUPPORT: fall through to the /etc/group
backend.  This keeps working on kernels that simply lack Unix domain
sockets, which is exactly the air-gapped CAOS configuration.
--- a/src/passwd/nscd_query.c
+++ b/src/passwd/nscd_query.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 
 	fd = socket(PF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM | SOCK_CLOEXEC, 0);
 	if (fd < 0) {
-		if (errno == EAFNOSUPPORT) {
+		if (errno == EAFNOSUPPORT || errno == ENOSYS) {
 			f = fopen("/dev/null", "re");
 			if (f)
 				errno = errno_save;
